# Tagging

A paragraph is a `P`, and a [link](https://example.org/spec) is both an
annotation on the page and a `Link` in the tree.[^why]

## Lists

- An item is an `LI` wrapping an `LBody` wrapping a `P`.
- Nesting opens a second `L` rather than a second document.

> A quoted list is an `L` inside a `BlockQuote`:
>
> 1. First.
> 2. Second.

## Cells

| Tag | Means |
| --- | --- |
| TH | Heading cell |
| TD | Data cell |

:::mdv-figure{caption="One Figure, carrying the alt text the chart was given." id=fig-tags}

```mdv bar
title: Tags per page
desc: A bar chart of tag counts on the first two pages, 12 then 9.
x: page
y: tags
---
page,tags
1,12
2,9
```

:::

:::mdv-callout{type=note title="Labels are printed"}

The label of a callout is an `H6`, because status is never colour alone.

:::

```ts
const tag = 'Code';
```

[^why]: A footnote body is a `Note`, set at the foot of the page that
    references it.
